<title>USA: TABLE - Maxcor Financial Q2 net income down.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Maxcor Financial Q2 net income down.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Maxcor Financial Group Inc</p>
<p>				     For the Three Months Ended</p>
<p>				  Jun 30, 1997	   Jun 30, 1996</p>
<p>				   (unaudited)	    (unaudited)</p>
<p> Total Revenue		$ 43,351,511	   $ 42,252,712</p>
<p> Net income			  107,056		1,148,062</p>
<p> Earnings per share		   0.01		  0.13(a)</p>
<p>Average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding		    8,949,656		8,949,656</p>
<p>					 For the Six Months Ended</p>
<p>				  Jun 30, 1997	   Jun 30, 1996</p>
<p>				   (unaudited)	    (unaudited)</p>
<p> Total revenue		  87,369,115	     91,086,173</p>
<p> Net income			1,141,003		4,601,237</p>
<p> Earnings per share		   0.13		  0.51(a)</p>
<p>Average shares</p>
<p>  outstanding		    8,949,656		8,949,656</p>
<p>NOTE: -- Company says Q2 earnings reflecting disappointing results from its London operations, where losses had the effect of offsetting overall profitability from the rest of its operations.</p>
<p>-- For comparative purposes, earnings per share information for the three month and six month periods ended June 30, 1996 is pro forma, presented as if all shares issued in Maxcor Financial's August 1996 acquisition of Euro Brokers had been issued and were outstanding for such period.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212 859-1700))</p>
</text>
